% ============================================================================
% sign-shape.query.adj — worked recall over the sign-shape library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to answer "what shape is a stop
% sign?" (direct), "which sign is the eight-sided one?" (REVERSE, and the
% question a child actually asks), or "which signs are rectangular?"
% (abstain — the MUTCD says regulatory signs are rectangular UNLESS
% SPECIFICALLY DESIGNATED OTHERWISE, and STOP and YIELD are two such
% designations, so the unqualified claim is one the manual never makes).
%
% It states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries.
%
% THE TABLE HOLDS A DEFAULT AND ITS OWN COUNTEREXAMPLES. STOP and YIELD are
% both REGULATORY signs and neither is rectangular; NO PASSING ZONE is a
% WARNING sign and is not a diamond. The rows only coexist because each
% default carries its defeasibility inside its atom. The bare-shape queries
% below are what prove that has not been quietly dropped.
%
% NOTE ON THE ABSTAIN QUERIES: they are written in VARIABLE form. A
% fully-bound query that matches nothing produces NO recall entry at all
% rather than an abstention, so the ground form would silently prove
% nothing.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli sign-shape.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "sign-shape.adj"

? sign_shape(stop_sign, $S)              % expect octagon
? sign_shape(yield_sign, $S)             % expect downward_pointing_equilateral_triangle
? sign_shape($Sign, octagon)             % expect stop_sign (REVERSE -- "which one is the eight-sided sign?")
? sign_shape(regulatory_sign, $S)        % expect rectangular_unless_specifically_designated_otherwise -- the hedge rides in the atom
? sign_shape(warning_sign, $S)           % expect diamond_shaped_unless_specifically_designated_otherwise
? sign_shape(no_passing_zone_sign, $S)   % expect pennant_shaped_isosceles_triangle -- a WARNING sign that is not a diamond
? sign_shape($Sign, rectangular)         % expect abstain -- the UNQUALIFIED claim, which the manual never makes
? sign_shape($Sign, diamond_shaped)      % expect abstain -- same, for warning signs
? sign_shape(speed_limit_sign, $S)       % expect abstain -- governed by the default, but the default is DEFEASIBLE; inferring its shape is reasoning, not recall
